### Units, signs, frames, and ordering
The bug-prevention rules. Sign, unit, coordinate, and ordering conventions are where silent errors
hide; define each once, here, and cite this section whenever a result is surprising.
- **Units & scales:** {{UNITS_TABLE}}
  <!-- per quantity: name · symbol · unit · plausible range -->
- **Sign & direction conventions:** {{SIGN_CONVENTIONS}}
  <!-- positive directions, axis orientations, the sign of any projection; the ONE definition the
       whole pipeline obeys -->
- **Coordinates & ordering:** {{COORDINATE_CONVENTIONS}}
  <!-- array index order (row/col vs x/y), pixel-center vs corner, canonical catalog ordering -->
- **Frame hygiene.** Name every frame; one symbol per axis per frame; state the frame of every
  gradient, derivative, and projected component. Resolve orientation and handedness from an
  independent geometric reference, never from the fit. Depth and the frame-consistency checklist:
  the physkit plugin's `docs/reference/coordinate-frames.md`.
- **Data layout & key arrays:** {{DATA_LAYOUT}}
  <!-- shapes and dtypes of the main arrays, what each axis means, masked/NaN handling -->

