## Durable decisions
<!-- GUARDED tier, append-only: never rewrite a closed entry; supersede it and link the two. -->

The durable **"why"** record for the whole project: decisions that outlive any one campaign — data
conventions, promoted-artifact choices, tooling / environment calls, cross-campaign methodology —
**plus the change log for this document's guarded sections** (§Mission and §Standing constraints
changes land here as entries). Losing this rationale on a copy or fork is what causes work to be
repeated; keep it here so it survives. (Campaign-scoped decisions live in that campaign's
`campaign.md` §Decision record.)

Each entry: the decision, the alternatives, why this one, the conditions it rests on, and what
would make you revisit it (mirrors the `record-decision` skill).

