### Version bumps & promotions

Two kinds of one-liners, both logged here. **A version bump** — a routine fix that does not
invalidate prior findings (a data or metric correction that preserves rankings) — is logged inside
its campaign's row history as `<campaign>` · `<date>` · `metric_version 1→2` · `<why>`. **A
promotion** — an artifact one campaign froze for the whole project to share (a validated forward
model, a generated training set) — is logged as `<artifact + version>` · `<date>` · `<from
campaign/session>` · `<project dir it now lives in>`; the promotion line here is what marks a
project-level artifact as promoted-frozen rather than working.

